{:edb/db-before-t 462 :edb/db-after-t 463 :edb/tx-data [[13194139533775 50 #inst "2026-10-04T22:18:27.840Z" 13194139533775 true] [17592186175978 1020 #edb/ref 17592186250271 13194139533775 true] [17592186175978 1020 #edb/ref 17592186250278 13194139533775 true] [17592186175985 1020 #edb/ref 17592186250257 13194139533775 true] [17592186175985 1020 #edb/ref 17592186250264 13194139533775 true] [17592186176271 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533775 true] [17592186176271 1145 "First, let's recall the graph of $y=\\operatorname{sec}⁡x.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13942972/assets/fbf6ef1ca91f998ab4dc2dda1890ffc8a713f2eeff19e5569351b2466256d63a.png)\n\nNotice that our graph is symmetric about the $y$-axis. If we reflect the graph about the $y$-axis, we get the same picture. This means that $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x$ is an *even* function, and we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sec}⁡(-x)=\\operatorname{sec}⁡x.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sec}⁡(-a) & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡a \\\\  & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533775 true] [17592186250257 1017 #edb/ref 17592186250258 13194139533775 true] [17592186250257 1089 "q-158049" 13194139533775 true] [17592186250257 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533775 true] [17592186250257 1100 "If $\\operatorname{sec}⁡a=\\sqrt{7},$ then $\\operatorname{sec}⁡(-a+20\\pi )=$" 13194139533775 true] [17592186250257 1113 #uuid "f9d793a4-ed3e-56ac-92ce-7b4313dd241b" 13194139533775 true] [17592186250257 1145 "First, let's recall the graph of $y=\\operatorname{sec}⁡x.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13942972/assets/fbf6ef1ca91f998ab4dc2dda1890ffc8a713f2eeff19e5569351b2466256d63a.png)\n\nFrom the graph, we note the following:\n\n- The period of $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x$ is $2\\pi .$\n\n- Our graph is symmetric about the $y$-axis. This means that $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x$ is an *even* function, and we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sec}⁡(-x)=\\operatorname{sec}⁡x.\n$$\n\nLet's now evaluate our expression:\n\n- Firstly, using the periodicity of $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sec}⁡(-a+20\\pi ) & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡(-a+2\\pi \\cdot 10) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡(-a).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Secondly, using the evenness of $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sec}⁡(-a) & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡a \\\\  & =\\sqrt{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\operatorname{sec}⁡(-a+20\\pi )=\\sqrt{7}.$" 13194139533775 true] [17592186250258 1000 #edb/ref 17592186250259 13194139533775 true] [17592186250258 1000 #edb/ref 17592186250260 13194139533775 true] [17592186250258 1000 #edb/ref 17592186250261 13194139533775 true] [17592186250258 1000 #edb/ref 17592186250262 13194139533775 true] [17592186250258 1000 #edb/ref 17592186250263 13194139533775 true] [17592186250258 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533775 true] [17592186250258 1041 "selection" 13194139533775 true] [17592186250258 1104 #edb/ref 17592186250261 13194139533775 true] [17592186250258 1110 #uuid "f16938f3-027a-5145-8bbb-97644bb31c1e" 13194139533775 true] [17592186250259 1034 "\\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{7}" 13194139533775 true] [17592186250259 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533775 true] [17592186250259 1111 #uuid "00ae29a7-0dbc-564c-a947-56886602f7d2" 13194139533775 true] [17592186250260 1034 "-7" 13194139533775 true] [17592186250260 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533775 true] [17592186250260 1111 #uuid "277e420e-a5db-580c-a84e-f42ec3b56ace" 13194139533775 true] [17592186250261 1034 "\\sqrt{7}" 13194139533775 true] [17592186250261 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533775 true] [17592186250261 1111 #uuid "42e4db29-12d2-5d31-8e0e-049e6f59d03d" 13194139533775 true] [17592186250262 1034 "7" 13194139533775 true] [17592186250262 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533775 true] [17592186250262 1111 #uuid "1e87649b-6131-5a33-8f89-55e576475a20" 13194139533775 true] [17592186250263 1034 "-\\sqrt{7}" 13194139533775 true] [17592186250263 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533775 true] [17592186250263 1111 #uuid "60bfb2ab-2037-5210-ad84-5459557acec7" 13194139533775 true] [17592186250264 1017 #edb/ref 17592186250265 13194139533775 true] [17592186250264 1089 "q-158053" 13194139533775 true] [17592186250264 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139533775 true] [17592186250264 1100 "If $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x=-\\frac{5}{3},$ then $6\\operatorname{sec}⁡(-x+8\\pi )+7=$" 13194139533775 true] [17592186250264 1113 #uuid "a8817eeb-ad4b-51b9-be15-71e5a745e14f" 13194139533775 true] [17592186250264 1145 "First, let's recall the graph of $y=\\operatorname{sec}⁡x.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13942972/assets/fbf6ef1ca91f998ab4dc2dda1890ffc8a713f2eeff19e5569351b2466256d63a.png)\n\nFrom the graph, we note the following:\n\n- The period of $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x$ is $2\\pi .$\n\n- Our graph is symmetric about the $y$-axis. This means that $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x$ is an *even* function, and we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sec}⁡(-x)=\\operatorname{sec}⁡x.\n$$\n\nLet's now evaluate our expression:\n\n- Firstly, using the periodicity of $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sec}⁡(-x+8\\pi ) & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡(-x+2\\pi \\cdot 4) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡(-x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Secondly, using the evenness of $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sec}⁡(-x) & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡x \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6\\operatorname{sec}⁡(-x+8\\pi )+7 & =6(-\\frac{5}{3})+7 \\\\  & =-10+7 \\\\  & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533775 true] [17592186250265 1000 #edb/ref 17592186250266 13194139533775 true] [17592186250265 1000 #edb/ref 17592186250267 13194139533775 true] [17592186250265 1000 #edb/ref 17592186250268 13194139533775 true] [17592186250265 1000 #edb/ref 17592186250269 13194139533775 true] [